   209	  - **The keys, exactly:**
   210	    - `question_id`: c01 to c15, each once;
   211	    - `no_view`: boolean;
   212	    - `reference`: `text` (string), `value` (finite number or null), `items` (list of ids);
   213	    - `implied_outcome`: `text` (string), `low` and `high` (finite numbers or null), `yes_no` (boolean or null), `items` (list);
   214	    - `direction`: above, in_line, below, yes or no;
   215	    - `confidence`: high, medium or low;
   216	    - `decisive_items`: a list;
   217	    - `against`: an object with `text` (string or null) and `items` (list), or null;
   218	    - `reasoning`: a string;
   219	    - `outcome_on_due_day`: present for an event only, absent for a figure; one of that question's rung labels, or null when `no_view`.
   220	  - **When `no_view` is true,** every other field may be null or empty.
   221	  - **Otherwise:**
   222	    - `reference.text`, `implied_outcome.text` and `reasoning` are non-empty;
   223	    - a figure has `low` ≤ `high` (both numbers), `yes_no` null, and `direction` above, in_line or below;
   224	    - an event has `yes_no` a boolean, `low` and `high` null, `direction` yes or no consistent with `yes_no`, and `outcome_on_due_day` consistent
