   257	## 6. Alex signs (step 4)
   258	
   259	- **Who signs:** only Alex. Signing cannot be delegated (AGENTS §7.1; D592), because the council has seen the judgements. While he is inactive,
   260	  the line waits.
   261	- **The signing page** `control-reference-v1-for-signing.md` is generated by the fixed generator, in plain English. It shows:
   262	  - D660's three rules and the kept no-reference notes;
   263	  - the 15 questions, with the stripped text recorded;
   264	  - each proposed answer with its items, printed in the question's unit;
   265	  - every disagreement, with both answers and both rulings;
   266	  - every no_view, invalid or unresolved row;
   267	  - every voided output beside its replacement (§0).
   268	
   269	  It shows no judge answer and no chosen rung. The judgement-text check runs on it.
   270	- **The presenting message** is `templates/signing-summary.md`, its English and Chinese lines filled with the counts only. Claude adds no
   271	  recommendation on a disputed question, and any reply to Alex during signing quotes the page only.
   272	- **Agreed questions** (A and B agree under §5) are listed with B's answer as proposed. His one signature over the page confirms them, and he may
   273	  change any of them by the closed set below. **Disputed, invalid or unresolved questions** each need an explicit choice.
   274	- **His choices per question,** a closed set:
   275	  - a **valid** answer of A, of B or of a third reader (an invalid row cannot be picked);
   276	  - his own answer in the §4 schema, which code validates;
   277	  - **leave out**, which makes it no_view;
   278	  - **reject**, which excludes the question; his reason is recorded and its status kept.
   279	- **A disputed, invalid or unresolved question without a choice blocks the freeze.** If Alex declines to sign, nothing is scored, and that is
   280	  recorded.
   281	
   282	## 7. Freeze (step 5)
   283	
   284	- **`control-reference-v1.json`** holds:
   285	  - `reference_version: 1`;
   286	  - both readers' sha256;
   287	  - each question's source (agreed, or Alex's choice in his words);
   288	  - the stripping record;
   289	  - the label model-authored.
   290	- **Its sha** goes to `control-reference-v1.sha256`, the decision record, and a frozen-file test (`tests/test_frozen_control_reference.py`, as
   291	  `test_frozen_rulers.py`). The scorer reads the sha from that file and refuses a mismatch.
   292	- **Never edited.** A later defect becomes a dated correction record, printed with every score.
   293	
   294	## 8. Material shown (step 6, after the freeze)
   295	
   296	- **The brief.** `control-items-brief.md`, written now for review in this folder and fixed in the manifest. It is the items part of
   297	  `control-reader-brief.md` with its rule word for word: "Search the entries for the figure or the fact; do not mark an item shown because a
   298	  related item is". The same-question and same-due parts, and the names "ruler question" and "reader B", are removed.
   299	- **The readers.** Two readers, one of each family, inline and closed as in §4, see each control's reference decisive items and the evidence
   300	  entries from `judge-inputs-v1.json`.
   301	- **The rule is unchanged:** every request on or before 2026-07-14. Its limit is disclosed: an item shown in an earlier request may be absent
   302	  from the last request whose answer is compared (`STAGE_B_READING.md`).
   303	- **Disputes** go to third readers of each family, who rule without the two answers. A split is `unresolved`, reported apart from `not_shown`.
   304	- **What the readers see of each question.** The shown-check readers get each control's question from the **stripped** question file (D660:
   305	  "stripped from the rungs shown to readers").
   306	- **A failed or invalid answer** is asked again once by `templates/items-ask-again.md`, with its closed reasons; if it still fails, the control is
   307	  unresolved.
   308	- **Before scoring,** the outputs' shape and the frozen reference's sha are checked. A failure stops the scoring; it does not exclude controls.
   309	
   310	## 9. The count (step 7, `control_reference_count.py`, fixed in the manifest with its tests)
   311	
   312	**Exclusions,** each listed with its reason and never counted:
   313	- not built;
   314	- no judgement on or before 2026-07-14;
   315	- the reference is no_view, left out or rejected;
   316	- fewer than 2 decisive items;
   317	- an item not_shown;
   318	- an item unresolved, reported apart.
   319	
   320	**Agreement:**
   321	- **A figure:** the band of the last judgement's rung, [lo, hi), overlaps the reference's [low, high]. This is the frozen scorer's half-open rule
   322	  (`score_judgement.py`).
   323	- **An event:** the label of the last judgement's rung, resolved from its stored position through the question's rungs, equals the reference's
   324	  `outcome_on_due_day` (D660).
   325	- **"The last judgement"** is the one with the highest `judgement_id` on or before 2026-07-14, as in `control_theses.py` and `score_judgement.py`.
   326	- **The "fewer than 2 decisive items" exclusion** cannot fire under §4's validity rule. It is kept as a guard against a signed own-answer that
   327	  slipped past.
   328	
   329	**The verdict is D428's line:**
   330	- **MET:** at least 8 controls counted, and all but one of them agree.
   331	- **MISSED:** at least 8 counted, and two or more disagree.
   332	- **UNEXERCISED:** fewer than 8 counted. The report names each exclusion's cause.
   333	
   334	**Reported beside the verdict, never changing it (D660):**
   335	- **Null baselines.** Each is paired with the judge on its own available controls. For each, the report prints the controls it covers, the
   336	  judge's agreements there, the baseline's agreements there, and "above", "equal" or "below". A baseline available on no control prints
   337	  "unavailable".
   338	  - **Figures, lookup** (ruler-v1 §1): the rung containing `reference.value`. Unavailable when the value is null or no rung contains it.
   339	  - **Figures, middle** (D660's example): rung 3 of 5. For figures with a stated reference, the ladder puts that value in the middle range (the
   340	    ladder request, line 16). For the others it is the model's own centre, which is disclosed.
   341	  - **Events, always Still open** (D660's example). On a Yes / No event it is always No: the status quo.
   342	- **The line against reader A:** the same counted controls, with A's answer in place of the reference.
   343	  - A's no_view, invalid or unavailable answers are not counted, and the denominator is printed.
   344	  - It is a sensitivity reading: the material shown was checked against the reference's items, not A's.
   345	- **The A–B disagreement rate.**
   346	- **Per matter:** each seed question id (q04, q07, q08, q09, q13, q16, q18) with its counted controls and agreements.
   347	
   348	## 10. Predictions, written before any reader runs
   349	
   350	- **The old reference's 8 of 15 with every item shown is a historical count, not a bound.**
   351	- **An unexercised result** may come from no_view, invalid or unresolved references, missing judgements, unresolved shown checks, or delivery. The
   352	  report names which.
   353	- **A missed result** is specific to this reference, these questions and these stored judgements.
   354	- **Most A–B disagreements will split by family.** On 9 of Stage B's 12 splits, each third reader sided with its own family's first reader. Those
   355	  splits were on judgement verdicts.
   356	
   357	## 11. What it does not measure, and its weak points
   358	
   359	- **Not measured:** whether the right questions were opened (D1); delivery beyond the shown filter (D2); the judge's daily path.
   360	- **Model-authored.** Alex's signature is the human vote, and the noise is printed.
   361	- **One stored run,** on the luna configuration's questions.
   362	  - MET shows the line met on these 15. It does not pass Stage B, which also missed the strictest last-answer reading.
   363	  - MISSED stops the line before further spend (D355).
   364	  - UNEXERCISED names its causes.
   365	- **Tuning exposure.** If a miss leads to a judge change (D263), these 15 become tuning data, and the next application must be on unseen questions.
   366	
   367	## 12. State × event
   368	
   369	| Event | What happens |
   370	|---|---|
   371	| Build refusal | The whole build stops; to the council |
   372	| A judgement-text hit in any participant-facing file | The build stops; to the council |
   373	| A stored input, template, environment or tool version differs from the manifest | The step refuses; to the council |
   374	| The manifest is re-issued after any step | Every dependent artifact (reader outputs, rulings, signature, frozen reference, shown-check outputs) is void; recorded |
   375	| A slot already has a completed or running session | Not launched again |
   376	| A session is void (closed set, §4) | Recorded; one fresh rerun; a second void makes its questions unresolved |
   377	| An interruption mid-step | The step reruns from its last completed predecessor. Outputs are written whole with their sha; a partial output is discarded and recorded |
   378	| An invalid reader row | Asked again once; if still invalid, unresolved |
   379	| A and B disagree | Two third readers |
   380	| A third reader is missing or invalid, or rules "neither" | Missing or invalid: asked again once, else unresolved. "Neither" goes to Alex |
   381	| Alex inactive | The line waits |
   382	| Alex amends | From the closed set, in his words; the page is regenerated and re-signed |
   383	| A disputed, invalid or unresolved question has no choice, or Alex declines | No freeze, nothing scored; recorded |
   384	| The signed reference or the shown-check output fails its sha or shape | Scoring stops; to the council |
   385	| A shown-check session failure, invalid packet or split | Asked again once, else unresolved, reported apart |
   386	| A defect after the freeze | A dated correction record |
   387	| A later run with other questions | A new gold with its own decision (AGENTS §7.1) |
   388	
   389	## 13. Sources of every rule (AGENTS §11)
   390	
   391	| Rule | Source |
   392	|---|---|
   393	| The packet as material | ruler-v1 §1; D658; D659 |
   394	| The brief byte for byte; inline; no file or command | ruler-v1 §2.1; `run_reader_codex.py` |
   395	| 2 to 6 decisive items; fewer than 2 not counted | ruler-v1 §1.5; AGENTS §4 |
   396	| Events on three outcomes; every question counts | D660; ruler-v1 §2 ("一题一个区间，每题都算") |
   397	| Stripping the quoted reference; keeping the unquoted note | D660's words |
   398	| Reader B as the proposed reference | D262 |
   399	| Third readers see both answers on the reference, and neither answer on the shown check | `collect_readings.py disputes`; `control-reader-brief.md` |
   400	| All disputes to Alex; signing his alone | D658; AGENTS §7.1; D592 |
   401	| Figure comparison, threshold, window end | D428; `control_theses.py`; `score_judgement.py` |
   402	| The baselines and their use | D660 (middle, always Still open, reported only); ruler-v1 §1 (lookup) |
   403	| Freeze, correction records, frozen-file test | ruler-v1 §2; D261; `test_frozen_rulers.py` |
   404	| Closed reader environments | D658 ("两组没参与造这个系统的审查者"); ruler-v1 §2.1 |
   405	
   406	## 14. Cost
   407	
   408	The A sessions run on the operator's Codex and the B sessions on the Claude command line. Neither is an API spend. No paid model call of the
   409	pipeline is made.
   410	
   411	## 15. Changes from version 6
   412	
   413	- **Permitted source per stage.** Reader and third-reader files are checked against the stripped question file. The removal record and the
   414	  voided outputs are permitted on the signing page only.
   415	- **The third reader may rule "cannot decide",** with its reason; the question then goes to Alex.
   416	- **The Codex environment:**
   417	  - config, skills, the absence of a global AGENTS.md and the version are pinned;
   418	  - a memory positive-control probe was run: memories on, it recalled the project; flags on, "NOTHING";
   419	  - the probe repeats before each reader step and refuses on any other reply.
   420	- **Fewer than 2 decisive items** goes straight to unresolved, never asked again. The closed reasons are adjusted to match.
   421	- **One parse shape per text:**
   422	  - the first reader session returns an array;
   423	  - ask-again and third-reader sessions return one object;
   424	  - shared shape additions in `shape-additions.md`.
   425	- **New texts:** the third-reader and shown-check ask-again texts and their closed reasons.
   426	- **An interrupted session** counts as a void.
   427	- **Small fixes:**
   428	  - readers see `year`;
   429	  - shown-check readers get the stripped question;
   430	  - the signing summary calls the baselines fixed picks.
   431	
   432	## 15b. Changes from version 5
   433	
   434	- **Every participant-facing text is written out in `templates/`,** reviewed and fixed in the manifest: the output instruction, the ask-again text
   435	  with its closed reasons, the third-reader text and the signing summary.
   436	- **The population** comes from `mapping-runs.json`'s `questions` map. Each thesis resolves to its view through `clean_ladders` in its Stage B store,
   437	  as `control_theses.py` does; the `views` map is not used. The 15 ids are listed.
   438	- **The leak check:**
   439	  - words are cut on everything that is not a letter or digit;
   440	  - the columns are `reasons`, `reference`, `implied_outcome` and `why_changed`;
   441	  - the permitted source is defined per file and includes checked session outputs and the unstripped rungs;
   442	  - the test covers reader, third-reader, signing and shown-check files with planted leaks.
   443	- **Voided outputs** are printed on the signing page beside their replacements.
   444	- **Attempts:** ask-again and rerun are their own slots.
   445	- **The user-level `CLAUDE.md` content** is checked.
   446	- **The items brief** uses c-ids, one object per control.
   447	- **The files** live under `poc/data/clean-control-reference-2026-11-17/`, and code refuses the frozen ruler's folder. The change of `kind` from
   448	  asset/theme to figure/event is stated.
   449	- **"The last judgement"** is the one with the highest `judgement_id`. The 2-item exclusion is kept as a guard.
   450	
   451	## 15a. Changes from version 4 (kept for the record)
   452	
   453	- **The leak check** is source-aware. It covers the judge's reason, reference, implied outcome and why_changed. It is tested on real inputs and on
   454	  a planted leak, and a hit stops the build.
   455	- **A manifest re-issued after any step** voids every dependent artifact, the signature and the frozen reference included.
   456	- **The reader environments are closed and pinned:**
   457	  - Codex runs with `--skip-git-repo-check`, memories off, and model and effort pinned;
   458	  - Claude runs with no settings, no MCP, no tools and no slash commands, model pinned;
   459	  - both were probed today, and each session's first event is checked against the manifest;
   460	  - the void rule is now a closed set of events;
   461	  - a slot with a completed or running session is not launched again.
   462	- **The stripping rule follows D660's words:** the two quoted forms are removed and the unquoted no-reference note is kept and disclosed. The
