     6	 "answer_with_ruling": "- `answer` must be null unless the ruling is \"neither\".",
     7	 "answer_missing": "- with the ruling \"neither\", `answer` must hold your own answer in the shape the brief gives.",
     8	 "answer_shape": "- your own answer does not fit the shape: {detail}",
     9	 "unknown_item": "- `{item}` is not an item id in the packet."
    10	}

FILE review-v7/templates/third-reader-ask-again.md
     1	# One ruling, made afresh
     2	
     3	An earlier ruling on question {question_id} did not fit the shape asked, for these reasons:
     4	{reasons}
     5	
     6	Read the question, the packet and the two answers above, and rule afresh. Return one JSON object for question {question_id}, in the shape asked above, and nothing else. Do not read any file or run any command: everything you may use is in this message.

FILE review-v7/templates/third-reader.md
     1	# Your task: a third reading of one question
     2	
     3	Two analysts answered the question above independently, from the same brief and packet you have above, and their answers disagree. They are shown below as Answer 1 and Answer 2, in an order drawn at random. Read the question and the packet yourself, then rule which answer the material supports:
     4	- "1" when Answer 1 is the one the material supports;
     5	- "2" when Answer 2 is;
     6	- "neither" when the material supports neither; then give your own answer in the shape the brief gives, with the additions below;
     7	- "cannot decide" when the material does not let you choose between them, for example when it supports both; say why.
     8	
     9	Cite item ids for your ruling. Return one JSON object and nothing else:
    10	{"question_id": "{question_id}", "ruling": "1" | "2" | "neither" | "cannot decide", "why": "two to four sentences, every claim with item ids", "answer": your own answer object when the ruling is "neither", otherwise null}
    11	
    12	{shape_additions}
    13	
    14	Do not read any file or run any command: everything you may use is in this message.
    15	
    16	## Answer 1
    17	{answer_1}
    18	
    19	## Answer 2
    20	{answer_2}

codex
**Version 7 still needs changes before the build.** The third reader can now say “cannot decide,” but some retry messages reveal the earlier reader’s conclusion, so the fresh reading is not blind.

For example, “with the ruling ‘neither’, `answer` must hold your own answer” tells the next reader how the earlier reader ruled. The items retry similarly reveals an earlier `not_shown` mark when explaining a missing reason. Use shape-only retry reasons that do not disclose the previous judgment. [Third-reader retry reasons](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/review-v7/templates/third-reader-ask-again-reasons.json:5), [items retry reasons](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/review-v7/templates/items-ask-again-reasons.json:7).

- **Stripped quotation:** The stage-specific source lists are improved, but the eight-word check alone still cannot guarantee that a removed quotation stays out of a reader prompt. The quotation may also occur in the permitted packet, so reintroducing it into a choice would pass that check. Compare the rendered question fields directly with the stripped question file. [Design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/review-v7/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v7.md:127), [D660](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9267).

- **Parse shape:** The design says the object parser takes the first `{…}`, while the items brief asks for one object **per control** or **per disputed item**, one per line. For a packet with multiple controls or disputes, that parser would read only the first unless the sessions are explicitly limited to one control or point. Define and test the full JSON-lines parser, or send one control or point per session. [Parser](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/review-v7/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v7.md:14), [items brief](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/review-v7/control-items-brief.md:20).

- **Interrupted session:** A start without an end does not establish that the process stopped; it may still be running. Check or reconcile the session’s actual state before marking it interrupted and launching its one rerun, so two readers cannot run for the same slot. [Design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/review-v7/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v7.md:202).

The Codex configuration, skills and memory flags are now pinned, and the memory probe provides a useful control. Its “NOTHING” response is evidence from that probe, not proof that no relevant context can ever reach a reader; keep the stated isolation checks as the governing boundary. [Design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/review-v7/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v7.md:167).

NOT READY: Keep retries blind, verify rendered questions against stripped inputs, and close the multi-object parsing and interrupted-session rules.
